# Animation candidate review

For every new or repaired animation candidate in this project:

- Deliver a GIF showing every candidate frame in its original order, plus a numbered contact sheet.
- State frame count, per-frame timing, loop behavior, source version and any preview-only transformations.
- Do not substitute static images or automated metrics for human visual review.
- Preserve original PNGs and alpha. GIF palette/background limitations are preview-only.
- Do not add, omit, mirror, interpolate or accelerate frames to conceal defects.
- If preview alignment is necessary, also provide an unaligned source-order preview and disclose offsets.
- Use only a common nearest-neighbor display scale; do not fit individual frames differently.
- Idle reference holds are labeled separately and never counted as transformation frames.
- A request to continue or approval of an action proposal is not approval of the resulting art.
- Stop on obvious deformation; present evidence for human review before generating more frames.
- Do not integrate candidates into the running App or formal atlas before the required approval.

Example: deliver `keyposes-4-frames.gif`, `contact-sheet.png`, and timing/alignment metadata with status `PENDING_USER_REVIEW`.
